[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  Mara's eyebrows lift slightly as you reach into your pack and pull out the 
  brass compass. The copper light catches its worn face as you hold it out to 
  her. She doesn't move to take it. Her gaze flicks from the compass to your 
  face, and something shifts in her expression — not suspicion, but a flicker 
  of... recognition? Concern? "That compass." Her voice is quieter now. "I've 
  seen you twist it in your fingers when you're thinking. You've had it a long 
  time, haven't you?" She still doesn't reach for it. "Kael — I asked you to 
  trust me, and I meant it. But I'm not going to take something that's been 
  with you through..." she gestures vaguely, "...whatever brought you to a city 
  with a sealed ash gate. Not like this." She holds your gaze, steady. "Keep 
  it. For now. If the moment comes when I *need* it, I'll tell you. But I'd 
  rather have your eyes and your wits than a trinket in my pocket." She taps 
  the charcoal rubbing again. "Now — that symbol. Look at the breaks. Seven of 
  them. Seven nights. Seven somethings passing through. You see the pattern?" 

