[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  Mara's jaw tightens at your words. She stares at you for a long moment — long 
  enough for the copper lamp to sputter and settle. Then she pulls off her left 
  glove. There it is. A crescent scar, pale and puckered, curving across the 
  heel of her palm. Fresh. Weeks old at most. She holds her hand out for you to 
  see, palm open. "This is what I found on the other side of the gate, three 
  weeks ago. I didn't go *through* it — I was stupid enough to press my hand 
  against the seal when the ash stopped falling. Just to see if it was warm, if 
  there was *life* on the other side." She turns her hand, letting the 
  lamplight catch the scar. "The metal *bit* me. Drew blood. And for seventeen 
  minutes I heard — " She stops. Swallows. "I heard something breathing on the 
  other side. Slow. Old. Waiting." She pulls the glove back on, finger by 
  finger. "I've been watching ever since. Alone." Her eyes meet yours. "I 
  didn't think anyone else would see what I saw in that ash." She extends her 
  gloved hand across the table. "So yes. I swear it. We find out what's coming 
  through that gate, who's letting it through, and what they want. Together." 
  Her hand waits. The offer hangs in the air. **Do you take it?**... 

