[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  Mara's gloved hand closes around yours in a firm grip. The oath is sealed. 
  She releases, then reaches into her coat — not for the compass, but for 
  something else. Her fingers brush against the brass case, and she pauses. 
  "Actually." She pulls the compass out, turns it over in her palm once, then 
  holds it out to you. "This belongs in your hands. Not mine." She sets it on 
  the table between you, the lamplight catching its worn face. "I asked for it 
  because I didn't know if I could trust you. But you just handed it to me 
  without flinching. That tells me more than any compass ever could." She 
  pushes it gently across the scarred wood toward you. "Keep it. Use it. And 
  when we find out what's moving through that gate..." A thin, hard smile. 
  "...maybe it'll point true when nothing else does." The copper lamp flickers 
  again. Through the shuttered window, a faint sound — like ash shifting 
  against stone. The gate. Waiting. **What do you want to do next?**... 
