[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  The smoke still curls from the cratered table when you hear it. Footsteps. 
  Heavy boots on wet cobblestones. Multiple sets. Coming fast. Mara sees it in 
  your face before you speak. Her eyes go narrow, her hand tightening on her 
  belt. "What—" "Patrol. At the door." She doesn't ask how you know. Doesn't 
  hesitate. She's already moving — snatching her coat collar up, sweeping the 
  charcoal rubbing off the table and into her sleeve in one fluid motion. She 
  doesn't touch the coins. Doesn't grab a bag. Doesn't look back. At the rear 
  of the tavern, a narrow door — warped wood, rusted hinges. She shoves it 
  open. Cold air and the smell of wet stone flood in. She pauses in the 
  threshold. Just long enough to meet your eyes. Her voice is a razor. "Find me 
  at the Drowned Bell when the dust settles. Don't let them see your face." 
  Then she's gone. The door swings shut behind her. The latch *clicks*. The 
  footsteps outside stop. A fist pounds on the front door. Three heavy knocks. 
  A muffled voice: "Finch! Open up — patrol check!" The tavern keeper — a grey 
  man behind the bar — looks at you. His eyes flick to the smoking ruin on the 
  table. Then back to you. The silence stretches. **What do you do?**... 

